${h}${h} Data product overview

This repository is the **instantiated data product** created from the **GCP Oracle ERP → PostgreSQL DWH ingest** blueprint. It implements a governed pipeline: **read-only Oracle ERP** extraction (one **input port** per configured schema), **your** transformation in **`application/transform_hook.py`**, **JSON Schema** validation against the **output port** contract, and **dlt** load into **PostgreSQL DWH**.

#if($dpDescription && $dpDescription != "")
**Description:** ${dpDescription}

#end
- **Technical name:** `${dpName}`
#if($dpFqn && $dpFqn != "")
- **FQN:** `${dpFqn}`
#end
- **Domain:** `${dpDomain}`
- **Data product version:** `${data_product_version}`
- **Owner:** ${dpOwnerName} (`${dpOwnerId}`)

${h}${h} Use case

**In scope:** Consolidate the same logical **Oracle ERP table** from **multiple schemas** (or a single schema) into **one PostgreSQL DWH table**, with a stable **datastoreapi** column contract on the output port, secrets in **Secret Manager**, infrastructure as code (**Terraform**), and CI (**Publish** image, **Deploy** per environment).

**Your responsibility:** Map source rows to the output contract in **`application/transform_hook.py`**, keep secrets and Terraform variables accurate, and run or schedule the **Cloud Run Job** after each deploy.

${h}${h} Repository layout

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| **`descriptor/data-product-descriptor.json`** | **DPDS** contract: input/output ports, **lifecycleInfo** slots for each environment. The platform also injects a **`blueprint`** lineage object (blueprint version + resolved parameters). Fill the **output port column map** here; do not treat the rest of the generated descriptor as a free-form rewrite. |
| **`application/`** | Python ingest package; **`transform_hook.py`** is the main code you implement. |
| **`application/src/`** | Generic runner: descriptor parsing, Oracle extract, validation, **dlt** load (blueprint-owned; protected). |
| **`infrastructure/`** | **Terraform**: Cloud Run Job, IAM, secret wiring (listed Terraform files are protected). |
| **`Dockerfile`** | Image that runs **`python -m src.main`**. |
| **`.github/workflows/publish.yml`** | Build and push the runner image (tag or manual **`image_tag`**). |
| **`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`** | **Terraform apply** for one **environment** and one published **`image_tag`**. |
| **`.odm/blueprint/`** | Lineage sidecar: blueprint README and a snapshot of the manifest used at instantiate/update. |

